# WALKSYNC (STORY's BRIEF_FOR_BUILD_WalkSync; John 14:20 "the animation speed and movement speed not syncing",
# 14:55 chose x1.5 natural). The engine drives each Walk16 man's leg frame from the distance he has walked this
# move (one 16-frame cycle per stride below) and times the move so he covers exactly what his feet do, with the
# legs at walkPaceScale times the clip's own pace. TU costs and the rules do not change.
#
# strides, in tiles per 16-frame cycle: [rifle walk, pistol walk, crouched sneak, empty-handed]. Measured 17 Nov two
# ways that agree: the source clips' hip travel (1.31 / 1.97 / 1.89 / 1.56 at 1 tile = height / 1.56) and the
# foot spread on four rendered sheets (airborne, duke, destro, scarlett: 1.1-1.33 / 1.79-1.92 / 2.1-2.3 / 1.8-1.9).
# STORY's 0.83 for the rifle walk did not hold up against either.
walk16:
  strides: [1.28, 1.9, 2.0, 1.7]
  walkPaceScale: 1.5
